\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Morris–Lecar foci}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Write #{F} for #{\dot V} and #{G} for #{\dot n} in the
Morris–Lecar velocity of \ref{fnip-0005}, and write
#{u=(V-V_{3})/(2V_{4})}. The 4 partial derivatives are
##{\frac{\partial F}{\partial V}
   =\frac{1}{C_{\mathrm{M}}}\bigl(-g_{\mathrm{L}}-g_{\mathrm{K}}n
   -g_{\mathrm{Ca}}m_{\infty}(V)
   -g_{\mathrm{Ca}}m_{\infty}'(V)\,(V-E_{\mathrm{Ca}})\bigr),}
##{\frac{\partial F}{\partial n}
   =-\frac{g_{\mathrm{K}}(V-E_{\mathrm{K}})}{C_{\mathrm{M}}},}
##{\frac{\partial G}{\partial V}
   =\phi\Bigl(n_{\infty}'(V)\cosh u
   +(n_{\infty}(V)-n)\frac{\sinh u}{2V_{4}}\Bigr),}
##{\frac{\partial G}{\partial n}=-\phi\cosh u,}
with
##{m_{\infty}'(V)
   =\frac{1}{2V_{2}\cosh^{2}((V-V_{1})/V_{2})}.}
\ref{fnip-0025} gives #{n_{\infty}'(V)}. At an
[equilibrium](fnip-0014) one has #{n=n_{\infty}(V)}, so the summand
of #{\partial G/\partial V} that contains #{n_{\infty}(V)-n}
vanishes.}

\p{In the Hopf column at #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=60}, the eigenvalues
of the [Jacobian](fnip-0034) at #{(V_{R},n_{R})} are a complex
conjugate pair with negative real part, so that equilibrium is a
stable [focus](fnip-0035). At #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=100}, the
eigenvalues at #{(V_{*},n_{*})} are a complex conjugate pair with
positive real part, so that equilibrium is an unstable focus.
\citet{§3.3.1, pp. 52–53}{ermentrout2010mathematical}
forms this matrix from the 4 partial derivatives.}

