\p{The curves solve the linear equation
#{\dot y=Df(x_{*})y} in the coordinates of the displacement #{y}.
The velocity they linearize is the Morris–Lecar velocity of
\ref{fnip-0005} at the equilibrium named in the panel. The filled circle
marks the stable focus and the open circle marks the unstable focus,
the convention of
\citet{p. 103}{izhikevich2007dynamical}.
In the upper drawing #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=60}, and the two solutions
start at the displacements #{(2,0)} and #{(-1.5,0)}, the states
#{(V_{R}+2,n_{R})} and #{(V_{R}-1.5,n_{R})}. The middle drawing is
the voltage coordinate of the solution that starts at #{(2,0)}.
In the lower drawing #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=100}, and the two solutions
start at #{(0.4,0)} and #{(-0.3,0)}, the states
#{(V_{*}+0.4,n_{*})} and #{(V_{*}-0.3,n_{*})}.}
